    {
      "type": "note",
      "id": "jOyMf",
      "x": 6160,
      "y": 3200,
      "name": "Rationale Overview B",
      "width": 470,
      "height": 520,
      "content": "OVERVIEW B — UNIFIED ZONES / BY-PROJECT\n\nPosition (§9.7): Board + Overview are ONE surface. A mode toggle switches focus, and the Board rides on top as a collapsed strip so it keeps its primacy (§10.10). The Overview reads BY PROJECT — 'where does nadim stand?' — not by band.\n\nProvenance is the spine (§5.5.1): ◆ derived (git) / ✓ verified (in-sync doc) / ~ suspect (drifting doc), on every item. Suspect is AMBER, never the Board's drift red — 'may be out of date' must not read as 'this is wrong' (§9.8).\n\n'Blocked on you' is lifted into its own spotlight band — the declared bottleneck, unmissable, sourced from the real 'Unblocked by: Sobhi' strings (§9.10).\n\nWeek view = Movement (7d, git-derived) + Waiting-longest (age as pressure; the bars are duration, not a trend). No burndown, no velocity (§5.5.3).\n\n+ Optimises: 'where does each project stand' and 'what's blocked on me' in one read; provenance legible per row.\n− Sacrifices: by-project scatters a single band (all Ready) across cards; denser and less glanceable than by-band."
    },
