    {
      "type": "note",
      "id": "i2APum",
      "x": 0,
      "y": 5480,
      "name": "Rationale Fix Proposal",
      "width": 2080,
      "height": 170,
      "content": "FIX PROPOSAL & GATE (§5.2)\nThree states, because the fix is the exception not the rule. (1) FIXABLE / DC1: the edit is one character (#22→#23), so it is shown inline in its FULL LINE, not as a red/green block — and the stale “(verified 2026-07-13)” neighbour is actively FLAGGED amber, because the mechanical fix introduces a new inaccuracy the tool can't see (§5.2.1.2). Two files (HANDOFF + LEARNINGS) approve together. The gate reads consequential — accent top-rail, the write target in mono, the unstaged/undo truth stated — but is a single action, no dialog-on-dialog (§10.11, §10.14). (2) NO AUTOMATIC FIX is a real, common state that says WHY there's nothing to click: the remedy is authorship, not substitution (§5.2.1.4). (3) AFTER APPROVAL is honest (§9.11): the write lands unstaged; approval does NOT mark drift resolved — the next reconciliation decides, so the state is “written · awaiting re-check”, never a fake green “fixed!”."
    },
    {
      "type": "note",
      "id": "wJCZY",
      "x": 6160,
      "y": 3760,
      "name": "Rationale Overview A",
      "width": 470,
      "height": 520,
      "content": "OVERVIEW A — TABBED / BY-BAND\n\nPosition (§9.7): the Overview is a second TAB beside the Board (top tab bar), so the Board keeps its own full surface and 3-second scan untouched. Bands are arranged BY BAND (§9.9) as a read-only five-column board — answering 'what's ready / blocked ANYWHERE', across all projects at once.\n\nProvenance per card (§5.5.1): ◆ derived / ✓ verified / ~ suspect — suspect is amber, never the Board's drift red (§9.8).\n\n'Blocked on you' gets an 'on you' chip inside the Blocked column, and that column is ordered by AGE (age as pressure), so the bottleneck surfaces without leaving the band view (§9.10). Week view = the top Movement strip (7d, git-derived) + the age-ordered Blocked column — movement + age, never a burndown (§5.5.3).\n\n+ Optimises: 'what can I pick up anywhere' at a glance; the tab keeps the Board primary and uncompromised.\n− Sacrifices: a single project (nadim) is scattered across columns — 'where does nadim stand?' takes more eye-travel than Concept B's by-project view. Read-only: no +New, no drag."
    }
  ],
